        "insight_type": "recommendation",
        "position_hint": 0.5,
        "routing_tag": "surface",
        "salience": 0.7667,
        "text": "It comes down to this: The frame for a security review is 'what could go wrong if this assumption is wrong'. We've seen this play out at teams using Sentry. If you ignore that, you end up rebuildin\u2026",
        "tier": 2
      },
      "type": "Insight"
    },
